From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 18:35:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05117/11362] [outer-loop] exp5051: declare aggregation
 substrate -> clears DURATION_TOO_SHORT false-positive

E1 continuous-self-learning (exp5051, .463) was FLAGGED/quarantined by adversarial_verify
DURATION_TOO_SHORT: 28ms vs the 60s live-model floor. Investigation: FALSE-POSITIVE, not
fabrication. The experiment reads CACHED upstream verified-trace artifacts (exp5045), builds
a replay memory, and computes pre/post held-out accuracy via a memory-selector lookup =
aggregation-class compute. It carried a vestigial GGUF model_specs (path-resolved, never
loaded) and declared no inference_substrate, so the linter applied the strict live-model floor.

The underlying finding is honest + preserved: replay-memory self-learning REGRESSED held-out
accuracy -0.05 (pre 0.70 -> post 0.65, contamination_guard_passed) -- an honest negative.

Fix: declare inference_substrate=aggregation_from_upstream_artifacts + random_seed in both the
success and blocked artifact builders. Re-run -> adversarial_verify 0 flagged, finding intact.
known-issues: planner-template note so future PHASE E self-learning/replay tasks declare the
substrate (not a vestigial GGUF model_specs) per CLAUDE.md Inference-Substrate Discipline.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
